 "provenance": "Tibet 14 secret stage (world 2, level 13) normal exit 5,21 (object 5, which sets field_551, so the result is exit, not secret-exit), control-only from the spawn on the exact S700 core (engine s700-core-2). Tick numbers below count frames played, as show.ts --cut=N does. Start values: weaponTier 2 (the hook; choosing Tibet on the seal grants tier >= 2, cGame.method_75). Tibet 14 is entered from Tibet 13, which the Tibet 5 secret exit opens (web-port entrance [2,4,12]), so it can be played before the Tibet 6 ice hammer. The route only uses the hook, and the same controls give the identical result with weaponTier 8 (a revisit value). maxHealth 4 (no armor), lives 12 (campaign value of the old routes), 0 diamonds, 0 red diamonds. diving true (the diving item from the Bavaria 8 chest 20,12, behind a riddle room). The stage cannot be finished without it: the water source at 30,14 floods the basin x=26..32 rows 18-21 by about frame 80, and that basin is the only link to the exit area (rows 21-22 west). With diving false the same controls leave the hero stuck at 28,16-17. So a campaign that reaches this exit already has the Bavaria 8 diving item. Tibet itself is not strictly after Bavaria: the seal opens Bavaria at 10 and Tibet at 25 red diamonds (Define.worldPrices {0,10,25}, method_73). Route (cells and hook pulls follow the intent of the old port route tibet-14-normal-hook). Walk in and collect the row-12 diamonds 10..15,12 (ticks 44-69, 6 diamonds). Go down column 16 and collect 16,16 by stepping on it (tick 94, 7). Push the stone 17,16 two cells east to 19,16 (ticks 104, 115). Facing west from 17,16, 16,16, 15,16 and 14,16, hook the row-16 diamonds 15,16, 14,16, 13,16 and 12,16 from two cells away (diamonds 8-11, ticks 138-263). Push the stone on east from 19,16 to 23,16 (ticks 294-327, hero at 22,16) and wait there until about tick 465. Walk west to 13,16 (tick 505) and back east to 21,16 (tick 545). Seven 2-cell hook pulls facing east, thrown from 21,16 down to 15,16 and stepping one cell west after each, bring the stone from 23,16 to 16,16 (ticks about 550-825). From 14,16 facing west, a hook pulls the diamond 11,16 from three cells away (diamond 12, tick 883). At 15,16 an east throw with the stone adjacent at 16,16 pulls nothing (about tick 910). Step back to 14,16; a final 2-cell pull (about tick 967) moves the stone from 16,16 to 15,16 (tick 972). Walk west and collect 10,16 and 9,16 (diamonds 13-14, ticks 1029, 1034). Climb column 9 to 9,12, go east along row 12 to 16,12 and down column 16 to 16,16, now east of the stone (tick 1108). Go east along row 16 to 23,16, up column 23 to 23,13 and onto checkpoint 24,13 (active at tick 1168). Go down over plate 25,15 (tick 1178), east to 28,15, and down 28,16-17. Swim down the flooded basin to 28,21 (tick 1220). Walk into the grass at 27,21; it is cut and the basin water drains west into the lower corridor. Go west along row 21 to 22,21, down to 22,22, and west along row 22 to 16,22 under the ceiling traps without stopping (no hit, tick 1272). Go up to 16,21 and west through the lock cell 6,21 (tick 1316) to the exit 5,21 (tick 1320). The exit walk ends at -6,21 at tick 1354. Diamond tally: 6 on row 12 + 16,16 + 4 hooked (15..12,16) + 11,16 hooked + 10,16 + 9,16 = 14. The magic diamond lock at 6,21 (count 69) does not block in this S700 logic. method_296 (the level loader) case 12 writes -1 into the tile layer field_334 at the lock cell, and only stores field_157/field_158/field_156 (lock x, y, count). So the counter falls with each collected diamond (69 -> 55), and the hero walks through the cell with 14 diamonds. Health 4 -> 4, no deaths, no resets.",
